<title>FRANCE: HORSE RACING-PRIX D'ISPAHAN RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-PRIX D'ISPAHAN RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the Prix d'Ispahan for</p>
<p>four-year-olds and upwards colts and fillies run over 1.85 kms</p>
<p>at Longchamp on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Sasuru (ridden by Michael Hills)</p>
<p>2. Wixim (Thierry Jarnet)</p>
<p>3. Simon du Desert (Christian Hanotel)</p>
<p>6 ran.</p>
<p>Distances: Short neck, three lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Anthony Oppenheimer, trained by Geoff Wragg</p>
<p>in England.</p>
<p>Value to the winner: $94,276.</p>
<p>Pari-Mutuel (to a one franc stake): Win 2.20; places 1.40</p>
<p>1.60. Straight Forecast 5.50.</p>
</text>
